# Unsaved-changes guard (always-on)

**Non-negotiable:** a new or changed UI in `ui/src/**` where the user edits
fields and must press Save / Apply / Update must prompt before those edits are
lost (route change, back button, tab close, modal close).

Full spec and recipes: **`unsaved-changes-guard`** skill
(`.agent/skills/unsaved-changes-guard/SKILL.md`). Claude Code / OpenCode: invoke
it before claiming UI work done.

| Surface                               | Use                                                                              |
| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Page, settings card, editor, RHF form | `useUnsavedChangesGuard({ isDirty, onSave })` (`@/hooks/useUnsavedChangesGuard`) |
| Modal, sheet, inline editor           | `useGuardedClose` + `<UnsavedChangesDialog {...dialogProps} />`                  |
| `navigate()` right after a save       | `useRunUnguarded()`                                                              |

## Do not

- Hand-roll `beforeunload`, `useBlocker`, `window.confirm`, or a per-feature "leave?" dialog.
- Call `setOpen(false)` directly from Cancel / X / Esc on a dirty modal (use `requestClose`).
- Add `<BrowserRouter>`; the app uses `createBrowserRouter` so `useBlocker` works.

## Exempt (state why in the PR)

Autosave surfaces, filters/search, confirm/delete/OTP dialogs with no draft, chat
composers, guest drafts already persisted by `useOfflineFormDraft`.

Docs: `docs/architecture/unsaved-changes.md`.
